Chapter 1
Creativity and general problem
solving
There are many Things that a writer cannot control in the film indus-
try. What we can control are the ideas we choose for our scripts. The most
important ingredient in ন is a first-rate film idea. This may sound
〜, but in fact many very talented writers do not fulfil their potential to
write world-class scripts because they choose ideas which, while interesting
and バ felt, য়nately, are Ð not 传 original ò for
the ش competiビ, expensive medium of feature film, чly now
that feature film has to compete for market share with υ from an ever-
increasing number of platforms. Of course, we should all be ル
committed to the films we are writing, but there is no point in writing a script
